," ","7",".","3",")\\n","dump","(","5",","," ","6",".","2",","," ","7",".","3",")\\n","dump","(","6",","," ","6",".","2",","," ","7",".","3",")\\n","dump","(","7",","," ","6",".","2",","," ","7",".","3",")\\n","dump","(","9",","," ","5",".","6",","," ","7",".","3",")\\n","\\\"","\"",", ","\"","description","\"",": ","\"","Check"," bottom"," bands"," of"," slides"," ","4","-","7"," and"," ","9","\"","}"]},{"type":"chunk","time":1788943961185,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":0,"block":{"type":"reasoning","text":"Confirmed slide-2 problems:\n1. KPI top row labels appear ABOVE the KPI cards area? Actually the dump shows KPI numbers at y0=1.85 and label 规划面积/建成面积 at y0=2.59?? Wait kpi() layout: number y+0.14 (h .72) → label at y+0.9. KPI card row1 at ly=1.62: label 规划面积 should be at 1.62+0.9=2.52. Dump: '规划面积' at 2.59 x7.81 (top-right card label) — matches (KPI1 label), '建成面积' 2.59. Numbers '1.78' at 1.85 top row ✓. Second row KPI at y 3.72 (ly+1.9+0.2=3.72): numbers 8.9 at 3.95? that's y0 3.95 — but number text vertical center valign middle: at 3.72+0.14=3.86..4.58 y0 ~3.95? Wait y0 3.95 means box y from 3.95?? hmm 8.9 at y0=3.95 x7.78: that's the label?? No label危化品面积 at 4.69, so 8.9 at 3.95 is value KPI row2. Row2 y3.72 + .14 = 3.86 to 4.58; glyph y0 3.95 ok.\n\nBut notice something bigger: map card title '园区边界范围示意（经纬度）' at y0=6.08 and caption at 6.92! Right column: map card title at my0... y0 6.08 → so my0 ≈ 5.9?? With my earlier my0 formula my0=ly+2*ch2+0.4: ch2=1.9: 1.62+3.8+0.4=5.82; title y0 = my0+0.16+? cardTitle y+0.16 h0.46 with valign middle: glyph y 6.08?? 5.82+0.16=5.98 top, valign middle text within h .46: glyph ~6.0-6.3? y0 6.08 plausible. So map card 5.82..7.04 h1.22 as computed; caption at 6.92 — overlaps nearly footer 7.15. And polygon (no text) squeezed in ~ (6.67..7.04)?? Plot MY0 = my0+0.85=6.67, MH = 1.22-1.1=0.12 → tiny 0.12in-high squiggle + caption 6.92 likely colliding with polygon or below it at very bottom overlapping polygon region? caption y0 6.92 in area plot to 6.79: caption below plot — but plot itself basically nonexistent.\n\nAdditionally left info card value col: geographic coordinates spans x 3.0..5.98 → y-row width fine (< 6.3 card edge). But that was row 8 at y6.43; card ends 7.04; fine. Notice though the left card rows ended at 6.43+0.3=6.7 < 7.04 good.\n\nSo must fix map area. Let me also double-check KPI label/numbers orientation top rows: row1 numbers '1.78' y0=1.85 (kpi num at y+0.14=1.76..2.48, glyph 1.85 ✓), labels at 2.59 (y+0.9=2.52..2.86 glyph 2.59 ✓). But wait KPI1 is 规划面积 number 1.78 top-left of right column: number at x7.65..8.54 centered in card w 2.99 starting 6.6+... hmm rx=6.6 cw2=(6.183-0.2)/2=2.99: card1 x 6.6..9.59 center ~8.1; number x7.65..8.54 width .89 centered? number text centered in w cw2=2.99 starting 6.6 → center ~8.09 ✓.\nKPI labels row1: 规划面积 at x7.81 (card1 centered 8.09? text center x~8.1 within label box w cw2-0.2). ✓.\n\nPlan: redesign right side of slide 2 to give map real room and remove redundancy. Currently info card duplicates area numbers (规划面积1.78 rows) AND KPI cards duplicate them. Redundant design flaw: basic info list includes 规划/建成/危化/占比, and KPIs top-right show same four values. Better: left list shows 名称/主导产业/坐标/化工分区规划/占比/其他; right: two KPI highlight cards (规划面积、建成面积) + map card large below containing '危化品面积 8.9 / 占比 5' chips row + polygon.\n\nNew slide 2 right column:\n- ch2 = 1.5 (2 cards side by side at y1.62): 规划面积 1.78 / 建成面积 1.78 (labels & sub '化工分区 1.78'?)\n Actually kpi() shows number+label; good.\n- Between 3.24 and map? Put a strip card y3.3 h1.2: 危化品面积 8.9 · 化工企业占比 5 → make one wide card with 2 stat halves. card y3.3 h1.25.\n- Map card y4.7 h2.34 (to 7.04): title at 4.86; plot MY0=5.35; MW=rw-1.2=4.98; MH=1.0; caption y6.45; fits.\n\nCompute: rows y1.62 h1.5 & second? I'll do top row two KPIs h1.5: 1.62..3.12; wide card 3.3..4.55; map 4.7..7.04 h2.34. Title 4.86 (title block .5) plot MY0=5.4 MH=1.05: 5.4..6.45; caption at 6.52..6.8; card bottom 7.04 ok; footer 7.15 ok. \n\nKPI function param: kpi(slide,x,y,w,h,num,label,color). Keep number 30pt within h1.5: num y+0.1 h .6, label y+0.72... adapt inline instead of kpi(): I'll build custom small stat: number centered 26pt y+0.12 h0.6, label 10.5 y+0.7 h0.4. I'll add param smaller.\n\nLeft card: basic info list: reduce to 6 rows removing duplicate 规划面积/建成面积/危化品面积/占比 (moved right) — keep: 园区名称, 主导产业, 化工分区规划面积, 危化品面积, 化工企业占比, 地理坐标. Hmm still duplicates partially. Wait remove duplicates entirely from list to avoid duplication; list = 园区名称 / 主导产业 / 地理坐标 / 化工分区规划面积 1.78 / ... no. Better list non-duplicated attributes: 园区名称, 主导产业, 化工分区规划面积(1.78), 地理坐标 — plus note about危化 as text? The KPIs & second card give 危化品面积/占比. And list adds 危化品面积/占比 duplicates... acceptable? Visual duplication of same value twice on one slide is sloppy.\n\nFinal slide 2 info card rows (6): 园区名称 / 主导产业 / 化工分区规划面积 1.78 / 危化品面积 8.9 / 化工企业占比 5 / 地理坐标 — yes duplicates the four area KPIs, so drop the area KPI row and instead right column: one card of 2x2 area KPIs top (taller: ch 1.6 rows y1.62 & 3.38) then map card 5.05..7.04 (h ~1.99) still small for map. Ugh circular.\n\nResolution: Shift info-card content: remove duplicates from list by moving area KPIs to right as the main '面积构成' highlight, and enrich left list with remaining: 名称/主导/坐标 + add '化工分区规划面积'. Rows: 园区名称, 主导产业, 化工分区规划面积, 地理坐标 = only 4 rows → card can shrink to h4.0? We can vertically center left card content, giving bottom breathing space and reduce right column width? Actually simplest: make LEFT list keep 8 rows but DROP KPI area duplicates by removing KPI grid; instead right column becomes single tall card '关键指标' with 2x2 inner tiles (bigger) plus map impossible again.\n\nTime to decide: skip polygon mini-map (the weak element causing layout pain) and replace right area with a cleaner visual: '面积与占比' panel containing four big stat tiles (2x2) each tile has big number + unit + label, in one card; left list keeps 8 row